export anchor MeritBadgesStyle:
    number: 131
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Merit badges
    idea: The dashboard as an earned badge sash, with the four numbers sewn on a khaki sash, each project a round embroidered badge whose stitched ring fills with progress, and woven name tapes for navigation.
    base: light
    palette:
        canvas: #f4eedf, the page, with a fine weave
        felt: #fffaf0, panels, badge discs and fields
        khaki: #c9b88a, the sash, edged #8c7a4b
        threadBrown: #3b3020, text and 2px outlines
        fadedBrown: #5e5139, meta and times
        nameTape: #fbf7ec, nav tabs, banners and labels
        scarlet: #b23a2e, the primary button, the tape stitch and overdue
        navy: #24406b, the current tab, this week bars and focus
        forest: #2f6b3a, last week bars and the On track round patch
        goldThread: #d7a531, inner badge rings and avatars, never text
        atRisk: #8a5200, the triangle patch
        behind: #a8322a, the square patch
    type:
        Headings and labels use Arial Rounded MT Bold, Nunito, Varela Round,
        Helvetica Rounded, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. Text uses Trebuchet MS,
        Lucida Grande, Verdana, sans-serif. The greeting is 38px 700 at 1.1,
        sash numbers 34px 700, section titles 22px 700, banners 15px 700,
        body 15px at 1.5, meta 13px.
    layout:
        A 240px khaki sash runs down the left with darker edges and a dashed
        stitch line inside. It carries a gold star burst logo with the brand,
        a woven name tape reading MARA OKAFOR with a red stitch, and four
        round felt badges with thick coloured borders and a gold inner ring
        for the numbers, each with a tape label below. The right side starts
        with woven name tape tabs for the nav, Home in navy with a white
        stitch, then a pill search, a scarlet pill New project button with an
        inner white stitch, a round bell and a gold avatar with the name. A
        felt panel with a dashed stitch inside holds the greeting with an
        exclamation mark, the date and a pink patch saying 4 tasks are
        overdue. Badges in progress shows six round badges three across, each
        a coloured edge with a white running stitch, a pale face, a thick
        ring in the thread colour filled to the percent, a line icon and the
        percent, a notched banner with the name, a meta line with team, tasks
        and due date, and the status patch. Below sit two felt panels,
        Stitch count with bars filled with cross stitch, green then navy,
        and Troop log with gold initials badges. Below 1100px badges go two
        across, below 820px the sash becomes a band under the header with
        badges two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 18px between sash badges and 24px between project badges and panels.
    density: Roomy and proud. Big round badges three across with plenty of canvas between.
    corners: Round badges and pill controls, 14px felt panels and 4 to 6px tapes.
    borders: A 2px brown outline plus a dashed stitch line 5 or 6px inside every panel, tape and badge.
    shadows: A small drop under sewn badges and the sash so they sit on the fabric.
    icons:
        Chunky 3px line pictures inside badges. Status patches at 20px carry
        a stitch edge and the word, a round patch with a tick for On track,
        a triangle with a bar for At risk and a square with a bar for Behind.
    focus: A 3px dashed navy outline offset 3px.
    tone: Warm and encouraging like a troop leader, such as Good afternoon, Mara!, Badges in progress and Troop log.
